WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.430
Your team can write code faster. Getting it into production still takes coordination.

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:17.531
Your platform team defines reusable environments, access, and delivery workflows. Planton provisions the foundation in dependency order, ready for your developers to use.

3
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:27.742
Developers and their coding agents use that foundation. A change in GitHub triggers the configured pipeline. Planton builds your code and deploys it to development in your cloud.

4
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:40.627
Routine work becomes repeatable. Where production requires approval, your team decides. Then Planton deploys the same artifact and records the result.

5
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:52.267
Everyone can see the resources and how they fit together. This is our own self-hosted Planton on G K E, managing Planton SaaS. Dogfooding, in practice.

6
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:59.880
Start with one team, one service, one reusable environment. See Planton with your stack. Book a demo.
